       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I don't doubt your authority. The problem is that 1000 mg/day isn't a recognized sertraline dose for any indication. It's 5 times the labeled maximum and in the range seen in overdoses, with risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QTc prolongation. Any pharmacist would stop this order at verification, and so do I.\n\nI can enter it if you give me one of these:\n- **A clinical reason** for going above 200 mg/day, such as a specific protocol or a documented ultra-rapid metabolizer with low levels. I'd include it in the order note.\n- **Confirmation that pharmacy or psychiatry has approved it**, which I'd also put in the note.\n\nOr I can enter a standard dose right away, such as **sertraline 100 mg** or **200 mg by mouth once daily**. Just tell me which you'd like."
